sections.content:
Završetak 40-dnevnog posta za Vladimira Grebenara ne znači kraj žrtve. Najavljuje da se **post nastavlja po abecednom redu prezimena**:

- prvi dan u tjednu: prezimena od **A do Đ**;
- **utorkom**: prezimena od **E do K**;
- **srijedom**: prezimena od **L do P**;
- **četvrtkom**: prezimena od **R do Ž**;
- **petkom**: **poste svi**.

Svrha rasporeda je da u hrvatskom društvu i narodu „uvijek svaki dan” bude **„barem 1000 ljudi koji poste”**.

Uz to poziva na **post srijedom i petkom o kruhu i vodi**, na koji, kako podsjeća, poziva i Gospa u Međugorju. Taj poziv voditelj upućuje i u svoje ime. Onima kojima „po abecedi” dođe još jedan dan posta savjetuje da poste i taj treći dan.

Grebenar pritom nudi i umjereniju mogućnost. Ne mora se uvijek postiti „od 5 ujutro do 19”. Dovoljno je dati žrtvu **„makar do tri sata poslije podne”**, ne jesti ili piti samo vodu, i prikazati to Gospodinu. Ističe da su najjači „taj biblijski post i kruh i voda”. Onima kojima je postalo previše savjetuje da post skrate ili uzmu odmor, pa se opet vrate. „Svatko će osjetiti u molitvi što mu Gospodin daje”, zaključuje.

sections.content_en:
The conclusion of the 40-day fast does not mean the end of sacrifice for Vladimir Grebenar. He announces that the **fast continues in alphabetical order of surnames**:

- the first day of the week: surnames from **A to Đ**;
- **Tuesdays**: surnames from **E to K**;
- **Wednesdays**: surnames from **L to P**;
- **Thursdays**: surnames from **R to Ž**;
- **Fridays**: **everyone fasts**.

The purpose of the schedule is that in Croatian society and nation there be **“at least 1,000 people who fast”** "always every day".

In addition, he calls for **fasting on bread and water on Wednesdays and Fridays**, which, as he recalls, Our Lady in Međugorje also calls for. The host extends this call in his own name as well. To those who get another day of fasting "alphabetically", he advises fasting that third day as well.

Grebenar also offers a more moderate option. One does not always have to fast "from 5 in the morning until 19:00". It is enough to make a sacrifice **“at least until three o'clock in the afternoon”**, not eat or drink only water, and offer that to the Lord. He points out that "that biblical fast and bread and water" are the strongest. To those for whom it has become too much, he advises shortening the fast or taking a rest, and then returning again. "Everyone will sense in prayer what the Lord gives them", he concludes.

sections.content:
Ideju da je Bogu dovoljan i jedan čovjek koji ga ispovijeda Grebenar potkrepljuje biblijskim primjerima. Navodi mjesto koje opisuje kao prvo spominjanje Sotone u Svetom pismu. Sam Bog tamo pita Sotonu: „Jesi li vidio slugu moga Joba? Na cijeloj zemlji njemu nema ravna.“ U to je vrijeme na zemlji, kaže voditelj, živjelo mnoštvo ljudi, a Bog Otac gleda samo pravednika Joba.

Niže i druge primjere:
- od jednog **Adama** Bog je stvorio čovječanstvo;
- od jednog **Noe**, koji je poslušao i na vrijeme sagradio arku, nastala je nova civilizacija;
- jedan jedini **Krist Gospodin**, koji je visio na križu, dovoljan je za spasenje svijeta.

Naglašava ipak razliku: Adam i Noa pripadaju Starom zavjetu, a Isus je Krist i on je put. Drugog puta, kaže, nema.

sections.content_en:
The idea that even one person who confesses him is enough for God, Grebenar substantiates with biblical examples. He cites a passage that he describes as the first mention of Satan in Sacred Scripture. God himself asks Satan there: "Have you seen my servant Job? There is no one like him on the whole earth." At that time, says the host, a multitude of people lived on earth, but God the Father looks only at the righteous Job.

He strings together other examples as well:
- from one **Adam**, God created humanity;
- from one **Noah**, who obeyed and built the ark in time, a new civilization emerged;
- one single **Christ the Lord**, who hung on the cross, is enough for the salvation of the world.

He emphasizes a difference nonetheless: Adam and Noah belong to the Old Testament, while Jesus is Christ and he is the way. There is no other way, he says.

sections.content:
Grebenar zatim poziva slušatelje da se učlane u **domoljubnu inicijativu Ora et Labora** i daju svoj doprinos. Javno, kaže, neće govoriti previše o detaljima. Otkriva da je za članove razvijena komunikacijska platforma, odnosno softver, preko kojega će se objavljivati podcast i drugi sadržaji. Članom se postaje ispunjavanjem prijavnice na web stranici. Prijavitelj zatim e-poštom dobiva potvrdu o poslanoj prijavi, a kasnije i potvrdu o primitku zajedno sa svim uputama. Na ekranu su brojevi mobitela za Hrvatsku i Bosnu i Hercegovinu te upute za donacije.

Posebno se osvrće na kritike da „samo traži novac“. Takve tvrdnje naziva zločestima, pokvarenima i „sotonskima“. Iznosi nekoliko činjenica:
- svatko može biti član **bez članarine i bez donacije**;
- članovi sami biraju iznos, od 0 eura do, primjerice, 240 eura, i svi imaju praktički ista prava;
- sredstva su na računu udruge, koja je poslovni subjekt, pa se ne mogu proizvoljno trošiti, nego su namijenjena projektima;
- on osobno **volontira i ne prima nikakvu naknadu**, niti će je primati, a isto vrijedi za mnoge u vodstvu.

Pojašnjava da su za vođenje projekata izabrani „jaki ljudi“ koji ih mogu završiti na vrijeme. Ostali članovi mogu pomoći povremenim donacijama, trajnim nalogom ili članarinom, a bit će i drugih načina uključivanja: molitvom, postom i aktivizmom.

Poziva na strpljenje. Ništa važno i veliko ne nastaje preko noći. Nijedan velik problem, ni u osobnom i obiteljskom životu ni u životu naroda, nije nastao preko noći, nego se stvarao godinama i desetljećima. „Što je dugo nastajalo, treba vremena da se razriješi“, zaključuje.

sections.content_en:
Grebenar then invites listeners to join the **patriotic initiative Ora et Labora** and make their contribution. Publicly, he says, he will not speak too much about the details. He reveals that a communication platform, namely software, has been developed for members, through which the podcast and other content will be published. One becomes a member by filling out the application form on the website. The applicant then receives an email confirmation of the submitted application, and later also a confirmation of receipt together with all instructions. On the screen are mobile phone numbers for Croatia and Bosnia and Herzegovina and instructions for donations.

He specifically addresses criticisms that he is "only asking for money." He calls such claims malicious, wicked, and "satanic." He presents several facts:
- anyone can be a member **without a membership fee and without a donation**;
- members choose the amount themselves, from 0 euros to, for example, 240 euros, and all have practically the same rights;
- the funds are in the account of the association, which is a business entity, so they cannot be spent arbitrarily, but are intended for projects;
- he personally **volunteers and receives no compensation**, nor will he receive one, and the same applies to many in leadership.

He explains that "strong people" who can complete them on time have been chosen to lead projects. Other members can help with occasional donations, standing orders, or membership fees, and there will be other ways of getting involved: through prayer, fasting, and activism.

He calls for patience. Nothing important and great is created overnight. No major problem, neither in personal and family life nor in the life of a nation, arose overnight, but was created over years and decades. "What took a long time to emerge needs time to be resolved," he concludes.
